  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 222 PM EDT Wed May 27 2026\n\n- Chance of evening storms south/east of Grand Rapids\n\nSurface obs reveal a weak frontal boundary bisecting the Lower\nPeninsula roughly from Whitehall to Alma. Dewpoints are in the mid\n40s north of the boundary and mid 50s south of there. SBCAPE is\naround 500 j/kg but is progd to increase to around 1000 j/kg by\nlate afternoon. Thus we'll retain the low chance pops south of\nI-96 through the afternoon and early evening; severe storms are\nnot expected. However, some gusty winds are possible given DCAPE\nnear 900 j/kg.\n\n- Dry and mild Thursday into the middle of next week.\n\nan omega block will be in place for much of the next week with\nridging over the Great Lakes. This means little chance of rainfall\nand warmer than normal temperatures. High temperatures in the mid\nto upper 70s and lows in the lower to mid 50s are expected.\nDewpoints will be in the lower to mid 40s. Once the block breaks\ndown, a cold front is progd to move through next Thursday which\nshould be our next chance of rain.",
